{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>We did not touch you.</b> Since he said to them, 'and you hated me,' they answered him: if we sent you away — we did not touch you, and we sent you away in peace. It does not refer also to what follows — 'as we did not touch you' and 'as we did nothing with you but good.' As it is written: כי לא לנצח ישכח אביון תקות עניים תאבד לעד." "<b>You are now blessed of HaShem.</b> Lest you say, 'while you are making me swear, also make Ishmael swear with me' — therefore it says <b>you are now blessed of HaShem</b>: we need make only you swear, for <b>you are now blessed of HaShem</b> — the Holy One, blessed be He, decreed that you shall inherit the land. As it is written: ויהי אחרי מות אברהם ויברך אלקים את יצחק בנו."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:06:09.423015556Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}